COMMENT ON TABLE questionnaire IS 'LinkML class bdchm:Questionnaire. A Questionnaire is an organized collection of questions intended to solicit information from patients, providers or other individuals involved in the healthcare domain. They may be simple flat lists of questions or can be hierarchically organized in groups and sub-groups, each containing questions. The Questionnaire defines the questions to be asked, how they are ordered and grouped, any intervening instructional text and what the constraints are on the allowed answers. The results of a Questionnaire can be communicated using the QuestionnaireResponse. (FHIR)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN questionnaire.id IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:Questionnaire.id. The ''logical'' identifier of the entity within the system of record. The simple value of this attribute stands for an identifier of this data object within the system, it can be used as a reference from other objects within the same system (i.e. primary and foreign keys), and it should be unique per type of object. The same data object copied to a different system will likely have a different "id" in the new system since "id" values are system specific and do not represent persistent business identifiers. Business identifiers are assigned outside the information system and are captured in the "identifier" field. The "id" field is more likely to be a serially or randomly generated value that is assigned to the data object as it is created in a system.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN questionnaire.identity IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:Questionnaire.identity. A ''business'' identifier or accession number for the entity, typically as provided by an external system or authority, that are globally unique and persist across implementing systems. Also, since these identifiers are created outside the information system through a specific business process, the Identifier type has additional attributes to capture this additional metadata so the actual identifier values are qualified by the context that created those values. This additional context allows "identifier" instances to be transmitted as business data across systems while still being able to trace them back to the system of origin.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN questionnaire.name IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:Questionnaire.name. Name for this Questionnaire (computer friendly)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN questionnaire.title IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:Questionnaire.title. Name for this Questionnaire (human friendly)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN questionnaire.description IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:Questionnaire.description. Natural language description of the Questionnaire';
COMMENT ON COLUMN questionnaire.url IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:Questionnaire.url. Canonical identifier for this Questionnaire, represented as an absolute URI (globally unique)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN questionnaire.version IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:Questionnaire.version. The identifier that is used to identify this version of the questionnaire when it is referenced in a specification, model, design or instance. This is an arbitrary value managed by the questionnaire author and is not expected to be globally unique. For example, it might be a timestamp (e.g. yyyymmdd) if a managed version is not available. There is also no expectation that versions can be placed in a lexicographical sequence.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN questionnaire.publisher IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:Questionnaire.publisher. Name of the publisher/steward (organization or individual) of this Questionnaire';
COMMENT ON COLUMN questionnaire.copyright IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:Questionnaire.copyright. Textual description of any use and/or publishing restrictions';
COMMENT ON COLUMN questionnaire.copyright_label IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:Questionnaire.copyright_label. Copyright holder and year(s)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN questionnaire.language IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:Questionnaire.language. The language(s) in which questions are presented.';

