COMMENT ON TABLE drug_exposure IS 'LinkML class bdchm:DrugExposure. DrugExposures are records of a Person suggesting exposure to a medication. The source could be prescription, dispensing, medication administration records (MARs), or patient medication list.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN drug_exposure.id IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:DrugExposure.id. The ''logical'' identifier of the entity within the system of record. The simple value of this attribute stands for an identifier of this data object within the system, it can be used as a reference from other objects within the same system (i.e. primary and foreign keys), and it should be unique per type of object. The same data object copied to a different system will likely have a different "id" in the new system since "id" values are system specific and do not represent persistent business identifiers. Business identifiers are assigned outside the information system and are captured in the "identifier" field. The "id" field is more likely to be a serially or randomly generated value that is assigned to the data object as it is created in a system.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN drug_exposure.drug_concept IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:DrugExposure.drug_concept. The coded value for a drug. From RxNorm. The syntax for the enum may need work.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN drug_exposure.exposure_provenance IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:DrugExposure.exposure_provenance. A value representing the provenance of the DrugExposure record. From OMOP Drug Types.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN drug_exposure.refills IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:DrugExposure.refills. Intended refills at time of the prescription.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN drug_exposure.quantity IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:DrugExposure.quantity. To find the dose form of a drug the RELATIONSHIP table can be used where the relationship_id is ‘Has dose form’. If liquid, quantity stands for the total amount dispensed or ordered of ingredient in the units given by the drug_strength table. If the unit from the source data does not align with the unit in the DRUG_STRENGTH table the quantity should be converted to the correct unit given in DRUG_STRENGTH. For clinical drugs with fixed dose forms (tablets etc.) the quantity is the number of units/tablets/capsules prescribed or dispensed (can be partial, but then only 1/2 or 1/3, not 0.01). Clinical drugs with divisible dose forms (injections) the quantity is the amount of ingredient the patient got. For example, if the injection is 2mg/mL but the patient got 80mL then quantity is reported as 160. Quantified clinical drugs with divisible dose forms (prefilled syringes), the quantity is the amount of ingredient similar to clinical drugs. Please see [how to calculate drug dose](https://ohdsi.github.io/CommonDataModel/drug_dose.html) for more information.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN drug_exposure.days_supply IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:DrugExposure.days_supply. The number of days of supply of the medication as recorded in the original prescription or dispensing record. Days supply can differ from actual drug duration (i.e. prescribed days supply vs actual exposure).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN drug_exposure.sig IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:DrugExposure.sig. This is the verbatim instruction for the drug as written by the provider.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN drug_exposure.route_concept IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:DrugExposure.route_concept. Route of drug administration.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN drug_exposure.identity IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:DrugExposure.identity. A ''business'' identifier or accession number for the entity, typically as provided by an external system or authority, that are globally unique and persist across implementing systems. Also, since these identifiers are created outside the information system through a specific business process, the Identifier type has additional attributes to capture this additional metadata so the actual identifier values are qualified by the context that created those values. This additional context allows "identifier" instances to be transmitted as business data across systems while still being able to trace them back to the system of origin.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN drug_exposure.associated_visit_id IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:DrugExposure.associated_visit. A reference to the Visit that is associated with this record. References Visit.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN drug_exposure.associated_participant_id IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:DrugExposure.associated_participant. A reference to the Participant that is associated with this record. References Participant.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN drug_exposure.age_at_exposure_start IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:DrugExposure.age_at_exposure_start. The Participant''s age (expressed in days) at the exposure start date.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN drug_exposure.age_at_exposure_end IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:DrugExposure.age_at_exposure_end. The Participant''s age (expressed in days) at the exposure end date, if available. Otherwise equal to age_at_exposure_start.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN drug_exposure.exposure_status IS 'LinkML slot bdchm:DrugExposure.exposure_status. A value indicating whether the exposure described in this record is present, absent, historically present, or unknown for this individual patient.';

